    rule_desc = [[
Top 100 producers in the word are fighting each other for the championship, so the 24-hour battle of the adventurers begins now!
 
 [c][C74848] Rules: [-][/c]
 
 1. 24-Hour Challenge is composed of 24 stages. The rival to be matched of each stage is determined by your comprehensive Strength after resetting. The latter the stage, the stronger the rival.
 
 2. In the challenge, you can deploy Lv. 20 Karma and above. The side who has more views (which is determined by the Strength of company and Karma) wins. The winner has the rewards.
 
 3. Deploying Guardian can boost the Strength of company. Deploying the specified Guardian of each term can greatly boost Strength. Karma above level 20 can be Guardian.
 
 4. During the challenge, the attributes of deployed Karma will decrease, and the total decrease is depending on the corresponding Strength of the rival's deployed Karma; the decrease of each deployed Karma is depend on its sequence in the formation.
 
 5. The Karma decreased during the challenge cannot automatically restore after the challenge. The Karma cannot be deployed only when its attributes decrease to 0.
 
 6. You can use 30 different Karma at most in one round. Before resetting, the Strength of deployed Karma keeps the same even when you upgrade or evolve the Karma or increase stars for it.
 
 7. You can restart the battle you lost by Gems. When you restart it, the previous decrease and the deployment are cleared; you can change formation to continue.
 
 8. There is a manual resetting chance can be obtained at 5:00 each day (except the day the system is unlocked). After resetting[c][C74848], the current progress and unclaimed rewards will be cleared[-][/c].
 
 9. If you have cleared 12 stages and above in a round, after the resetting, you can quickly clear a third of previous cleared stages by using the relative function. With Privilege Card, you can clear half of that, [c][C74848]ignoring the decimal part[-][/c]. No attributes of Karma will decrease when you use that function.]]
